"text":"A cancel element indicates that the old key signature should be canceled before the new one appears. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"will always happen when changing to C major or A minor and need not be specified then. The cancel value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches the fifths value of the canceled key signature (e.g., a cancel of -2 will provide an explicit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation for changing from B flat major to F major). The optional location attribute indicates where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation appears relative to the new key signature.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLCancel/Location-swift.enum":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcancel\/location-swift.enum","title":"MXLCancel.Location","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel\/Location-swift.enum","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The cancel-location type is used to indicate where a key signature cancellation appears relative to a new key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signature: to the left, to the right, or before the barline and to the left. It is left by default. For mid-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure key elements, a cancel-location of before-barline should be treated like a cancel-location of left."}],"role":"symbol"}}}